All video related Quests usually send a stack trace with the progress reports. This means Discord would know exactly which functions were called, and can therefore verify that their own functions initiated the progress. Questify erases this stack trace, but the absence of it will be just as telling as its presence.

Play on Desktop, Play on PlayStation, Play on Xbox, and Play Activity Quests are only available on official desktop clients due to a limitation imposed by Discord. 3rd party clients such as web extensions, Vesktop, Equibop, and others, do not support auto-completing these Quest types.

All game related Quests usually send a game fingerprint with the heartbeat reports. This means Discord can use data from tens of thousands of users to determine whether other users are likely using a real game or are emulating the executable. There is no reasonable method to spoof this value, so Questify leaves it blank, but the absence of it will be just as telling as poorly spoofing the value.

Achievement in Activity Quests can only be auto-completed by completing them immediately. This method may be patched at any time.

Auto-completing Quests is done by clicking their respective buttons on the Quests page. Quests will be auto-completed in the order they were queued, unless the simultaneous completion setting is enabled above.

